# This file is part of vim-unit: Unit tests for vim imitators
#
# Scrolling: CTRL-E, CTRL-Y, CTRL-D, CTRL-U, CTRL-F, CTRL-B, zt, zz, zb, z<CR>,
# z. and z-, in the plain case only; the finer points of scrolling (and the
# 'scrolloff', 'sidescroll' and 'smoothscroll' options) are not tested. The
# tests use a 6-line window, start with the first line at the top, and observe
# the scroll position through where scrolling pushes the cursor and with H
# and L.

:start Scroll CTRL-E (cursor pushed off the top line)
:window 20x6
:set scrolloff=0 startofline
